model_answer:
Definition of Method Overloading:
 Method overloading occurs when multiple methods in the same class have the same name but different parameter lists (different number, type, or order of parameters). It is an example of compile-time polymorphism because the compiler determines which method will be executed.

Definition of Method Overriding: 
Method overriding occurs when a subclass provides a new implementation of a method already defined in the parent class using the same method signature. It is an example of run-time polymorphism because the method call is resolved during execution.

Comparison:
| Method Overloading                                              | Method Overriding                                              |
| --------------------------------------                         | ----------------------------------------                     |
| Happens within the same class                         | Happens between parent and child classes |
| Same method name, different parameters | Same method name, same parameters        |
| Compile-time polymorphism                            | Run-time polymorphism                                     |
| Inheritance not required                                     | Inheritance required                                             |





Example:

class Area {
    int calculate(int side) {
        return side * side;
    }

    int calculate(int length, int width) {
        return length * width;
    }
}

class Bird {
    void fly() {
        System.out.println("Bird flies");
    }
}

class Sparrow extends Bird {
    void fly() {
        System.out.println("Sparrow flies low");
    }
}

calculate() is overloaded and fly() is overridden..

